Are you all right?

246
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:49,957
Hang in there, man.

247
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:50,870
We got you, buddy.

248
00:14:50,953 --> 00:14:51,783
How's he doing?

249
00:14:51,866 --> 00:14:52,696
Akura.

250
00:14:52,779 --> 00:14:54,080
Hey, so where am I?

251
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:56,197
You're with your friends now, Akura.

252
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:57,737
He doesn't look very good.

253
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:59,957
I think we need to get him to a doctor.

254
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:02,037
So why don't we get
Kaiba to land this day?

255
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:06,473
Yeah, but first, help him onto my back
so that we can get him to his room.

256
00:15:08,220 --> 00:15:09,120
There you go.

257
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:15,160
I'm glad Bakura's okay.

258
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:18,477
That was one of the toughest
choices I ever had to make.

259
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:22,197
If the evil spirit didn't come back to
duel, I don't know what I would have done.

260
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:24,697
The Millennium Ring is
a lot like my puzzle.

261
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:28,737
It holds an ancient spirit that depends
on someone else so it can exist.

262
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:33,477
And even though the spirit of the ring is
evil and controls Bakura against his will,

263
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:37,060
it seems to still need
Bakura in order to survive.

264
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:42,320
But there's one major difference
between Bakura and Ayami. What's that?

265
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:45,020
The spirit inside my item is my friend.

266
00:15:45,460 --> 00:15:49,657
And you and I are always there to support
each other, no matter what comes our way.

267
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:52,397
You were there to help me when
my grandfather was in trouble.

268
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:57,897
And now, I'm here to help you rescue the
world from evil. I promise. Together,

269
00:15:57,980 --> 00:16:00,817
we'll figure out the secrets
of your ancient past and how

270
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:03,637
to unlock your hidden powers
before Merrick can take them.

271
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:08,580
Because your destiny is mine, too,
and we're going to win. That's right.

272
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:10,200
This was a tough duel,

273
00:16:10,380 --> 00:16:13,757
but thanks to our teamwork and the
heart of the cards, we came out on top.

274
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:17,317
Now we're headed for round two, and
we're going to take it all the way,

275
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:19,940
as long as we stick together. Right.

276
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:22,515
Nothing will keep us from our destiny.

277
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:23,810
Awesome!

278
00:16:27,660 --> 00:16:28,490
Hold on.

279
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:32,157
According to Battle City rules,
as the winner of the duel,

280
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:35,637
you are entitled to take the rarest
card from your opponent's deck.

281
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:38,760
So it's time to claim
your prize, Yugi. No way!

282
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,647
I think Bakura's been
through enough already.

283
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:45,736
So, Yugi won the first duel
of the Battle City finals.

284
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:46,920
I knew he would.

285
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:48,420
No surprise.

286
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:52,237
With a card as powerful as Slifer
the Sky Dragon in his deck,

287
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:53,967
Yugi is difficult to defeat.

288
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:55,290
Hmm.

289
00:16:55,373 --> 00:16:59,020
Unless, of course, his opponent
also has an Egyptian God card.

290
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:04,597
Bakura's been through a lot,
and he definitely needs rest.

291
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:07,677
But we gotta land this blimp
and get him to a hospital.

292
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:08,590
Yeah.

293
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:12,994
Some crazy stuff went down in that
duel, especially when Marek showed up.

294
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:15,400
What exactly happened back there?

295
00:17:16,380 --> 00:17:19,917
For some reason, Marek didn't want
the Spirit of the Ring to lose.

296
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,737
So when I was about to play my
Egyptian God card and win the duel,

297
00:17:23,820 --> 00:17:26,897
Merrick used his Millennium
Rod to free the real Bakura.

298
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:28,077
Since he was injured,

299
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:30,917
Merrick knew I would forfeit the
duel instead of attacking him.

300
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:34,177
But the spirit must have been
afraid I would attack Bakura,

301
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:37,280
because he took control
again at the end. So wait,

302
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:40,997
do you mean to tell me that the Dark
Spirit of the Millennium Ring let you win?

303
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:43,727
Yup, because he depends
on Bakura to survive.

304
00:17:44,020 --> 00:17:47,917
And if I attacked Bakura with Slifer,
the spirit might have been in danger too.

305
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:48,920
I'm confused.

306
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:53,257
Even though the evil spirit was in control,
you still ended up attacking Bakura.

307
00:17:53,340 --> 00:17:54,170
No,

308
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:57,857
since the evil spirit was in control
of Bakura when I attacked him,

309
00:17:57,940 --> 00:17:59,528
the real Bakura was spared.

310
00:17:59,700 --> 00:18:01,037
This is all so confusing,

311
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:05,061
but it sounds like Marek and the
evil spirit were in this together.

312
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:07,657
Yeah, but I'm not sure how or why.

313
00:18:07,740 --> 00:18:10,740
I just know we can't let
Marek win this tournament.

314
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:14,880
And hopefully, that evil spirit
won't be coming back again.

315
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:16,617
I don't know about you,

316
00:18:16,700 --> 00:18:20,759
but I've had enough of evil spirits
and mind controlling for one day.

317
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:23,220
I'm sick of that, Marek! Come on!

318
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:24,200
Let me at him.

319
00:18:24,420 --> 00:18:27,540
Hey, don't get yourself in
trouble again. All right.

320
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:29,977
I think it's time to talk
to Kaiba about getting

321
00:18:30,060 --> 00:18:32,877
Bakura back into the
hospital as soon as possible.

322
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:34,260
Yeah, Tristan's right.

323
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:36,197
Let's get some help for Bakura.

324
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:38,757
Then let's stop talking
about it already and go.

325
00:18:38,840 --> 00:18:39,670
Go ahead.

326
00:18:39,753 --> 00:18:41,777
I'll stay here and keep an eye on Bakura.

327
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:43,507
Okay, hang in there, Bakura.

328
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:44,778
Help is on the way.

329
00:18:46,980 --> 00:18:47,920
Hold on, guys.

330
00:18:48,180 --> 00:18:49,298
What's wrong, Yugi?

331
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:51,197
Everything all right?

332
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:52,700
It's gone. Huh?

333
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:54,170
What's gone?

334
00:18:54,660 --> 00:18:56,131
Bakura's Millennium Ring.

335
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:57,600
I don't get it, guys.

336
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:00,377
He had it around his neck
until the end of the duel.

337
00:19:00,460 --> 00:19:02,200
And now it's disappeared.

338
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:06,577
That thing seems to come and go all
the time without any explanation.

339
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:10,340
Yeah, and your Egyptian god card
properly blasted it sky high.

340
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:12,011
Now let's get going, huh?

341
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:13,541
Well, all right.

342
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:14,920
See you, Taya.

343
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:17,070
Later, guys.

344
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:25,060
Ha ha ha ha ha!

345
00:19:58,720 --> 00:19:59,940
Go, go, go.
